# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this exists: the repo has core.autocrlf=true and is edited on Windows.
# A shell script checked out (or re-committed) with CRLF fails on Linux with
#   bash: ./deploy.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
# which is a confusing failure to debug on a fresh VPS. Pinning these to LF
# means deploy.sh behaves the same no matter which machine touched it last.
#
# Only the extensions that actually break are listed — a broad `* text=auto`
# would rewrite the whole tree for no benefit.

# Shell scripts are executed by Linux (deploy.sh on the VPS).
*.sh text eol=lf

# This file itself — it warned about CRLF on its own first commit.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# YAML is read by Lavalink (Java) on Linux; LF avoids any parser surprises.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Explicitly mark the binary assets so Git never attempts text conversion.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
